Red at 917c70e:
  a-column-called-fih            "a list of values is still refused"
  the-schema-reader-was-blind-in-english
                                 "a shopping list holds things, not columns"
                                 "a list after a field noun holds that field's values"
  derivedColumns('A shopping list with milk, bread and eggs') -> [milk, bread, eggs]
  derivedColumns('a list of categories: coffee, tools, sweets') -> [coffee, tools, sweets]

Culprits (bisected): c219da21 (shopping list), 76f66a5d (categories).
Root cause - one rule, written once, lost twice (two readers that must
agree, maintained separately):
  c219da21 moved theListAnIntroducerHandedOver in FRONT of the container
    reader ("Add amount, category, date, and note" after "tracker"), and
    the introducer reader never learned that a bare «list» holds values.
  76f66a5d turned RECORD_CONTAINER's capture group into a non-capturing
    one (accusative forms, board/queue), so `holder[1]` became undefined
    and `!/^(?:list|قائمة)$/.test('')` always answered "holds columns" -
    the rule became dead code.
Decision: R. One function, aBareListHoldsValues(container, names), used
by both readers: the container reader asks it with holder[0]; the
introducer reader asks it with the container governing the introducer
(the last container before it in the sentence). c219da21's precedence and
its Pocket Ledger / tracker cases are kept (a tracker is not a bare list).
Added the negative half: a bare «قائمة» with definite Arabic names is
still his columns (the rule is for Latin items only).

Mutation evidence (mutate.py, sha256 identical after each):
  M3 introducer path without the rule:
    ✕ a list of values is still refused / ✕ a shopping list holds things
    Received: [{"key": "text1", "label": "milk", ...
  M4 container reader asks holder[1] again (the 76f66a5d state):
    ✕ a list after a field noun holds that field's values
    Received: [{"key": "text1", "label": "coffee", ...
  M5 rule applied to Arabic names too:
    ✕ a bare «قائمة» of definite names is still his columns
    - Expected - 5 / + Received + 1  ("الاسم","الصف","الدرجة" lost)

